    <main id="main-content">
        <section id="overview" class="hero">
            <p class="eyebrow">GAVEL backend</p>
            <h1>API documentation and integration reference</h1>
            <p class="lead">A complete reference for authentication, court cases, documents, public transparency data, pro-bono workflows, administration, and public contact reporting.</p>

            <div class="base-grid">
                <div class="base-url">
                    <span>Local base URL</span>
                    <code>http://localhost:1940/api/v1</code>
                </div>
                <div class="base-url">
                    <span>Production base URL</span>
                    <code>https://gavel-backend-nw0p.onrender.com/api/v1</code>
                </div>
                <div class="base-url">
                    <span>Browser documentation</span>
                    <code>http://localhost:1940/docs</code>
                </div>
                <div class="base-url">
                    <span>Health check</span>
                    <code>GET /health</code>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="quick-links" aria-label="Quick links">
                <a class="quick-link" href="#auth">Authentication setup</a>
                <a class="quick-link" href="#contact">Contact API</a>
                <a class="quick-link" href="#responses">Response contract</a>
                <a class="quick-link" href="#status-codes">HTTP status codes</a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="quick-start">
            <h2>Quick start <a class="heading-link" href="#quick-start" aria-label="Link to Quick start">#</a></h2>
            <div class="card">
                <pre><code># Install dependencies
npm install

# Seed demo users and sample cases
npm run seed

# Start with automatic reload
npm run dev

# Run the test suite
npm test</code></pre>
                <div class="callout">All seeded demo accounts use the password <strong>Password123!</strong>.</div>
                <div class="demo-grid">
                    <div class="demo-card"><span>Admin</span><code>admin@gavel.app</code></div>
                    <div class="demo-card"><span>Judge</span><code>judge@gavel.app</code></div>
                    <div class="demo-card"><span>Lawyer</span><code>lawyer@gavel.app</code></div>
                    <div class="demo-card"><span>Clerk</span><code>clerk@gavel.app</code></div>
                    <div class="demo-card"><span>Litigant</span><code>litigant@gavel.app</code></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <h3>Authentication and authorization</h3>
                <p>Protected routes require <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;accessToken&gt;</code>. Login also sets an HTTP-only <code>refreshToken</code> cookie, so browser clients should enable credentials. A refresh token may alternatively be sent in the request body.</p>
                <div class="badge-list" aria-label="Available roles">
                    <span class="badge">admin</span>
                    <span class="badge">judge</span>
                    <span class="badge">lawyer</span>
                    <span class="badge">clerk</span>
                    <span class="badge">litigant</span>
                    <span class="badge">public</span>
                </div>
                <pre><code>import axios from 'axios';

const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: 'http://localhost:1940/api/v1',
  withCredentials: true,
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }
});

api.interceptors.request.use((config) => {
  const token = localStorage.getItem('accessToken');
  if (token) config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;
  return config;
});</code></pre>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="cors">
            <h2>CORS origins <a class="heading-link" href="#cors" aria-label="Link to CORS origins">#</a></h2>
            <p>The backend accepts requests from <code>CLIENT_URL</code> and the following built-in development origins. Requests without an origin, such as curl, Postman, or native mobile clients, are also accepted.</p>
            <div class="card">
                <div class="badge-list">
                    <span class="badge">http://localhost:5173</span>
                    <span class="badge">http://localhost:3000</span>
                    <span class="badge">http://localhost:5174</span>
                    <span class="badge">http://localhost:8080</span>
                    <span class="badge">http://127.0.0.1:5173</span>
                    <span class="badge">http://127.0.0.1:3000</span>
                    <span class="badge">CLIENT_URL</span>
                </div>
                <div class="callout">When <code>NODE_ENV</code> is not <code>production</code>, other origins are permitted for local development.</div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="auth">
            <h2>1. Authentication <a class="heading-link" href="#auth" aria-label="Link to Authentication">#</a></h2>
            <p>Base path: <code>/auth</code>. Registration, login, verification, password recovery, and token refresh are public. Profile and logout operations require authentication.</p>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Access</th><th>Body</th><th>Behavior</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/auth/register</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td><code>{ firstName, lastName, email, password, role?, phoneNumber?, barNumber? }</code></td><td>Creates a volunteer lawyer account and attempts to send an email verification link.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/auth/login</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td><code>{ email, password }</code></td><td>Returns the user, access token, and refresh token; also sets the refresh-token cookie.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/auth/logout</code></td><td><span class="access">Authenticated</span></td><td>None</td><td>Clears the stored refresh token and cookie.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/auth/refresh-token</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td><code>{ refreshToken? }</code> or cookie</td><td>Rotates the refresh token and returns a new access/refresh pair.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/auth/me</code></td><td><span class="access">Authenticated</span></td><td>None</td><td>Returns the authenticated user's profile.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/auth/forgot-password</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td><code>{ email }</code></td><td>Sends a password-reset link. Always returns a neutral success message to prevent account enumeration.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/auth/reset-password/:token</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td><code>{ password }</code></td><td>Sets a new password using a reset token valid for 10 minutes and invalidates refresh tokens.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/auth/verify-email/:token</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td>None</td><td>Verifies the email. Browser requests redirect to <code>CLIENT_URL/login?verified=true</code>; API clients receive JSON.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/auth/resend-verification</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td><code>{ email }</code></td><td>Creates and sends a new verification link for an unverified account.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <h3>Public signup policy</h3>
                <p>Public self-signup is available only to volunteer lawyers. If <code>role</code> is omitted, the account is created as <code>lawyer</code>. Legal Aid Officers, Records Officers, administrators, and all other non-lawyer roles must be created by an administrator through <code>POST /users/invite</code>.</p>
                <div class="callout warning">Submitting <code>admin</code>, <code>judge</code>, <code>clerk</code>, or any other non-lawyer role returns <code>403</code>.</div>
                <pre><code>{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Public signup is only available for volunteer lawyers."
}</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <h3>Registration when verification email fails</h3>
                <p>The account is committed before email delivery is attempted. If SMTP delivery fails, registration still returns <code>201</code>; the failure is logged internally and the user can request a new verification email.</p>
                <pre><code>{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Account created, but verification email could not be sent. Please request a new verification email.",
  "data": {
    "user": {
      "_id": "...",
      "email": "lawyer@example.com",
      "role": "lawyer"
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <h3>Login response</h3>
                <pre><code>{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Login successful",
  "data": {
    "user": { "_id": "...", "firstName": "System", "role": "admin" },
    "accessToken": "eyJhbGci...",
    "refreshToken": "eyJhbGci..."
  }
}</code></pre>
                <div class="callout">Web clients should prefer the HTTP-only refresh-token cookie. The response-body refresh token supports clients that cannot use browser cookies.</div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="cases">
            <h2>2. Cases <a class="heading-link" href="#cases" aria-label="Link to Cases">#</a></h2>
            <p>Base path: <code>/cases</code>. Every route requires authentication. List results are automatically scoped so judges and lawyers only see their assigned cases.</p>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Access</th><th>Body or query</th><th>Behavior</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/cases</code></td><td><span class="access">Authenticated</span></td><td><code>?page=1&amp;limit=10&amp;status=Active&amp;stage=Trial</code></td><td>Returns a paginated and filterable case list.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/cases</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin / Clerk</span></td><td><code>{ caseNumber, title, description?, court?, stage?, status?, isProBono?, plaintiffs?, defendants?, detentionDate? }</code></td><td>Creates a case with a generated <code>GAV-YY-XXXXXX</code> hash ID.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/cases/export</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin / Judge</span></td><td><code>?format=csv</code> or <code>?format=pdf&amp;caseId=&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Downloads all cases as CSV or one case as PDF.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/cases/bulk-import</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin / Clerk</span></td><td><code>FormData: { file: .csv }</code></td><td>Creates cases from CSV. Required headers are <code>caseNumber</code> and <code>title</code>.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id</code></td><td><span class="access">Authenticated</span></td><td>None</td><td>Returns one case by MongoDB ID with lawyer and judge names/emails populated.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method patch">PATCH</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin / Clerk / Judge</span></td><td><code>{ title?, description?, court?, plaintiffs?, defendants? }</code></td><td>Updates general fields. Stage and status must use the dedicated status endpoint.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method delete">DELETE</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin</span></td><td>None</td><td>Permanently deletes the case and its complete status history.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id/status</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin / Clerk / Judge</span></td><td><code>{ stage?, status?, stallReason?, comments? }</code></td><td>Updates stage/status and creates an immutable audit-log entry.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id/audit-log</code></td><td><span class="access">Authenticated</span></td><td>None</td><td>Returns the full status-history timeline, including who changed what and when.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id/qr-slip</code></td><td><span class="access">Authenticated</span></td><td>None</td><td>Returns a Base64 PNG QR code linking to the public case page.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>Bulk import CSV</h3>
                <pre><code>caseNumber,title,court,stage,status,isProBono
FHC/001/2026,"Land Dispute Case","Lagos High Court",Pre-Trial,Active,false</code></pre>
                <div class="callout warning">The generic <code>PATCH /cases/:id</code> endpoint ignores stage and status. Use <code>POST /cases/:id/status</code> so the change is audited.</div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="documents">
            <h2>3. Documents <a class="heading-link" href="#documents" aria-label="Link to Documents">#</a></h2>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Access</th><th>Body</th><th>Behavior</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id/documents</code></td><td><span class="access">Authenticated</span></td><td>None</td><td>Lists all documents associated with a case, including each document's <code>fileUrl</code>.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id/documents</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin / Clerk / Lawyer</span></td><td><code>FormData: { file: File, description?: String }</code></td><td>Uploads a case attachment and returns its metadata.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method delete">DELETE</span></td><td><code>/documents/:id</code></td><td><span class="access">Owner / Admin</span></td><td>None</td><td>Deletes the database record and physical file. Only the uploader or an administrator can delete it.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="callout">Uploaded files are served from <code>/uploads</code>. Prepend the backend origin to <code>fileUrl</code>, for example <code>http://localhost:1940/uploads/&lt;filename&gt;</code>.</div>
        </section>

        <section id="public">
            <h2>4. Public data <a class="heading-link" href="#public" aria-label="Link to Public data">#</a></h2>
            <p>Base path: <code>/public</code>. No authentication is required. Public case responses use a strict field allowlist and never expose names, emails, lawyers, judges, or other personally identifiable information.</p>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Access</th><th>Behavior</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/public/cases/:caseHashId</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td>Returns <code>caseNumber</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>stage</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>court</code>, <code>filingDate</code>, <code>hashId</code>, and timestamps.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/public/scorecard</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td>Returns total, active, resolved, and stalled case counts plus resolution rate.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/public/backlog-map</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td>Returns active and stalled counts grouped by court, sorted by total backlog descending.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/public/trends</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td>Returns monthly items shaped as <code>{ period: "2026-01", filed: 5, resolved: 2 }</code>.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="callout warning"><code>/public/cases/:caseHashId</code> requires the public hash ID, such as <code>GAV-26-8A3F9</code>, not the MongoDB <code>_id</code>.</div>
        </section>

        <section id="watch">
            <h2>5. Watch subscriptions <a class="heading-link" href="#watch" aria-label="Link to Watch subscriptions">#</a></h2>
            <p>Public visitors can subscribe to case status updates by email.</p>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Access</th><th>Body</th><th>Behavior</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/watch/:caseHashId</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td><code>{ email }</code></td><td>Subscribes the email and returns an unsubscribe token.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method delete">DELETE</span></td><td><code>/watch/:idOrToken</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td>None</td><td>Unsubscribes using either the saved token or subscription MongoDB ID.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>Subscription response</h3>
                <pre><code>{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Successfully subscribed to case updates",
  "data": {
    "unsubscribeToken": "a3f9e2b1..."
  }
}</code></pre>
                <p>Save the unsubscribe token in the client so the user can later remove the subscription.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="pro-bono">
            <h2>6. Pro-bono <a class="heading-link" href="#pro-bono" aria-label="Link to Pro-bono">#</a></h2>
            <p>Base path: <code>/pro-bono</code>. Every endpoint requires an authenticated user with the <code>lawyer</code> role.</p>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Access</th><th>Query</th><th>Behavior</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/pro-bono/cases</code></td><td><span class="access">Lawyer</span></td><td><code>?minDetentionDays=30</code></td><td>Lists unrepresented pro-bono cases, optionally filtered by minimum detention days and sorted by longest detention.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/pro-bono/cases/:id/claim</code></td><td><span class="access">Lawyer</span></td><td>None</td><td>Claims a case, adds the current lawyer, and writes an audit entry. An already claimed case is rejected.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/pro-bono/my-claimed</code></td><td><span class="access">Lawyer</span></td><td>None</td><td>Lists pro-bono cases claimed by the current lawyer.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="analytics">
            <h2>7. Admin analytics <a class="heading-link" href="#analytics" aria-label="Link to Admin analytics">#</a></h2>
            <p>Base path: <code>/analytics</code>. All endpoints require the <code>admin</code> role.</p>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Access</th><th>Behavior</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/analytics/overview</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin</span></td><td>Returns total, active, and pro-bono case counts plus user totals and role distribution.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/analytics/heatmap</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin</span></td><td>Returns case counts grouped by court and stage, excluding closed cases.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/analytics/trends</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin</span></td><td>Returns monthly status-transition counts from <code>StatusHistory</code>.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="users">
            <h2>8. User management <a class="heading-link" href="#users" aria-label="Link to User management">#</a></h2>
            <p>Base path: <code>/users</code>. All endpoints require the <code>admin</code> role.</p>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Access</th><th>Body or query</th><th>Behavior</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/users</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin</span></td><td><code>?role=lawyer&amp;page=1&amp;limit=20</code></td><td>Returns a paginated list of users, optionally filtered by role.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/users/invite</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin</span></td><td><code>{ email, firstName, lastName, role, court? }</code></td><td>Creates a pre-verified account with a generated temporary password and attempts to email the invitation.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method patch">PATCH</span></td><td><code>/users/:id</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin</span></td><td><code>{ firstName?, lastName?, role?, phoneNumber?, isActive? }</code></td><td>Updates general user fields. Password changes are blocked on this endpoint.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method patch">PATCH</span></td><td><code>/users/:id/suspend</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin</span></td><td><code>{ reason? }</code></td><td>Suspends the user, invalidates existing access tokens, records the actor/reason, and blocks self-suspension.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method patch">PATCH</span></td><td><code>/users/:id/reactivate</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin</span></td><td>None</td><td>Reactivates a suspended account and records the administrator.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/users/:id/audit-log</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin</span></td><td>None</td><td>Returns the user's suspension and reactivation history.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="contact">
            <h2>9. Contact and issue reporting <a class="heading-link" href="#contact" aria-label="Link to Contact and issue reporting">#</a></h2>
            <p>Base path: <code>/contact</code>. Anyone can submit a message. Reading or updating the inbox requires an administrator.</p>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Access</th><th>Body or query</th><th>Behavior</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/contact</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td><code>{ name?, email, category, message }</code></td><td>Trims and validates input, saves the message, then attempts to notify the configured administrator.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/contact/messages</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin</span></td><td><code>?page=1&amp;limit=20&amp;status=new&amp;category=privacy_concern</code></td><td>Returns messages newest first with optional status/category filters and pagination. Maximum limit is 100.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="method patch">PATCH</span></td><td><code>/contact/messages/:id/status</code></td><td><span class="access">Admin</span></td><td><code>{ status, adminNotes? }</code></td><td>Updates inbox status and optional notes. Resolving records the administrator and resolution time.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <h3>Submit a message</h3>
                <pre><code>POST /api/v1/contact
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Optional sender name",
  "email": "sender@example.com",
  "category": "privacy_concern",
  "message": "Message text"
}</code></pre>
                <p><code>email</code>, <code>category</code>, and <code>message</code> are required. Every string is trimmed. Messages may contain up to 5000 characters.</p>
                <p class="mini-title">Allowed categories</p>
                <div class="badge-list">
                    <span class="badge">general_question</span>
                    <span class="badge">report_issue</span>
                    <span class="badge">privacy_concern</span>
                    <span class="badge">case_information_concern</span>
                    <span class="badge">volunteer_legal_aid</span>
                </div>
                <pre><code>{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Message sent successfully",
  "data": {
    "messageId": "..."
  }
}</code></pre>
                <div class="callout success">The database save happens first. If notification delivery fails, the failure is logged internally and the saved submission still returns <code>201</code>.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <h3>List the admin inbox</h3>
                <pre><code>GET /api/v1/contact/messages?page=1&amp;limit=20&amp;status=new&amp;category=privacy_concern
Authorization: Bearer &lt;adminAccessToken&gt;</code></pre>
                <pre><code>{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Contact messages retrieved successfully",
  "data": {
    "messages": [],
    "pagination": {
      "page": 1,
      "limit": 20,
      "total": 0,
      "pages": 0
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <h3>Update message status</h3>
                <p>Allowed statuses are <code>new</code>, <code>in_review</code>, <code>resolved</code>, and <code>closed</code>.</p>
                <pre><code>PATCH /api/v1/contact/messages/:id/status
Authorization: Bearer &lt;adminAccessToken&gt;
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "in_review",
  "adminNotes": "Optional note"
}</code></pre>
                <pre><code>{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Contact message updated successfully",
  "data": {
    "message": {
      "_id": "...",
      "status": "in_review"
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <h3>Email notification configuration</h3>
                <pre><code>CONTACT_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL=admin@example.com</code></pre>
                <p>The subject format is <code>[GAVEL Contact] &lt;Category Label&gt; from &lt;sender email&gt;</code>. The email includes the sender name or “Not provided”, sender email, category label, message, creation date/time, and message ID.</p>
                <p>SMTP delivery uses <code>EMAIL_HOST</code>, <code>EMAIL_PORT</code>, <code>EMAIL_USER</code>, <code>EMAIL_PASS</code>, and <code>EMAIL_FROM</code>.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="health">
            <h2>10. System health <a class="heading-link" href="#health" aria-label="Link to System health">#</a></h2>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Access</th><th>Behavior</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/health</code></td><td><span class="access">Public</span></td><td>Returns <code>{ status: "UP", timestamp: &lt;milliseconds&gt; }</code> for uptime and readiness checks.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="responses">
            <h2>Standard response formats <a class="heading-link" href="#responses" aria-label="Link to Response formats">#</a></h2>
            <p>Frontend integrations can consistently read <code>success</code> and <code>message</code>. Successful operations include <code>data</code> when they return a resource. Validation failures may additionally include field-level <code>errors</code>.</p>
            <div class="response-grid">
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Success (2xx)</h3>
                    <pre><code>{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Operation successful",
  "data": { }
}</code></pre>
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>General error (4xx / 5xx)</h3>
                    <pre><code>{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Error description"
}</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>Validation error (422)</h3>
                <pre><code>{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Validation failed",
  "errors": {
    "email": "Please provide a valid email address",
    "password": "Password must be at least 8 characters long"
  }
}</code></pre>
                <div class="callout warning">Development-mode server errors may include a <code>stack</code> field. Production responses do not expose stack traces.</div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="status-codes">
            <h2>HTTP status codes <a class="heading-link" href="#status-codes" aria-label="Link to HTTP status codes">#</a></h2>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Code</th><th>Name</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><code>200</code></td><td>OK</td><td>The request completed successfully.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>201</code></td><td>Created</td><td>A resource was created successfully.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>400</code></td><td>Bad Request</td><td>The request violates input or business rules.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>401</code></td><td>Unauthorized</td><td>The access token is missing, invalid, expired, or invalidated.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>403</code></td><td>Forbidden</td><td>The authenticated role is not allowed, or a public signup attempted a forbidden role.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>404</code></td><td>Not Found</td><td>The requested route or resource does not exist.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>422</code></td><td>Unprocessable Entity</td><td>Field validation failed; inspect the response <code>errors</code> object.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>429</code></td><td>Too Many Requests</td><td>The API rate limit was exceeded.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>500</code></td><td>Internal Server Error</td><td>An unexpected server error occurred.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <a class="top-link" href="#top">Back to top</a>
        </section>

        <footer>
            GAVEL API reference. All endpoint paths are relative to <code>/api/v1</code>.
        </footer>
